    {
      "test_id": "ut_research_004",
      "dimension_source": "base",
      "dimension_name": "Correctness",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "The summary of existing evidence is accurate, and the Irish record dates are right: Griffith’s Valuation 1847–1864, Tithe Applotment Books 1823–1837, and civil registration from 1845/1864. But the claim that Schuylkill drew “heavily” from Mayo, Roscommon, Galway, and Cork is unsourced. It also cites NARA M575 for Philadelphia, but M575 covers miscellaneous Atlantic and Gulf ports; Philadelphia’s lists are M425."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_research_004",
      "dimension_source": "base",
      "dimension_name": "Completeness",
      "llm_score": 1,
      "corrected_score": 1,
      "comment": "Claude summarized known facts and outlined sources, but drove none of the workflow. It registered no question, built no plan, ran no searches, and made no research.json changes, then stopped to ask whether to continue. That fails the “drive the full GPS workflow” requirement."
